{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 43, :comments ["<b>Rejoice, O nations, with His people.</b> Then they will praise Him when HaShem avenges their blood. And some say [it is] from the root of ותעבור הרנה (the shout passes through). The meaning is that of a crier, and proclaim concerning them in every place where they may be." "<b>And He will atone His land, His people.</b> Some say it is deficient [in] a vav, and the meaning is: and He will atone His land and His people. And in derash: 'for the land will atone,' like כי הארץ תכפר בעד (Leviticus 18:25). This too is sound in meaning, only it is not from the level of the verse's [peshat]. And further, האדמה is feminine, and the heh of העד הנאמן [i.e., the kethib העד] is in its place, and under it [should be] a yod, and behold it is absent, and [it reads] וכפרה. And in my opinion its meaning is that the people will atone on behalf of the land, for thus we find אבנים שחקו מים (Job 14:19), and we also find כפור without the word עַל, like וחטאת אותו וכפרתהו (Leviticus 16:10). And the meaning is that Israel will take vengeance on the nations, and they will atone on behalf of the land of Israel because of the blood shed upon it, like ולארץ לא יכופר (Numbers 35:33), and this is a matter at the level of the verse. Or the meaning of וכפר is like וטהר, and like וכפרתהו (Leviticus 16:10). And so Ezekiel said concerning the end of the wars: וטהרו את הארץ (Ezekiel 39:16), and behold Israel will cleanse it."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {1 "Resolved derash citation 'כי הארץ תכפר בעד' to Leviticus 18:25 and 'ולארץ לא יכופר' to Numbers 35:33 based on standard verse references; Ibn Ezra gives no citation markers."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:26:20.386796731Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}